<h2>Questions</h2>
<h3>How safe is the password account?</h3>
<p>
  Passwords are stored only as scrypt hashes, sign-in attempts are limited, and without signing in
  nothing leaves your browser at all.
</p>
<h3>What happens when I'm offline?</h3>
<p>
  TabCabin keeps working from the browser's own database. Changes wait and are sent when the
  computer is back online.
</p>
<h3>Can I stop syncing later?</h3>
<p>
  Yes. Sign out in Settings → Account & sync. The boards stay in the browser; they just stop
  syncing.
</p>
